-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/60a13fb7-b5f6-42c8-a0c6-5776b68eddeb
-- title:
--   Exact rational exponential endpoints for a height-one theta certificate
-- statement:
--   Define a table of 494 exact rational triples $(x_i,\ell_i,u_i)$, indexed by $i\in\{0,\ldots,493\}$. The displayed Lean data give every rational numerator and denominator explicitly. These arguments and endpoints are used to bound elementary exponentials in a 99-cell integration certificate for the height-one theta-energy witness.
--
--   This definition only records rational data. It does not assert that $\ell_i\le e^{x_i}\le u_i$. That mathematical assertion is stated and proved separately for every one of the 494 rows.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `MasulloRH.HeightOneExponentialTable.entries` is an array of triples in $\mathbb Q^3$; `MasulloRH.HeightOneExponentialTable.entry : Fin 494 → ℚ × ℚ × ℚ` uses an explicit proof that its index is in bounds. There are no padded rows, default endpoints, floating-point values, or hidden numerical assumptions. The first, second, and third coordinates are respectively the exponential argument, lower endpoint, and upper endpoint.
-- source:
--   Original rational endpoint certificates generated for the explicit height-one theta-energy witness, https://prove2.me/theorems/89c50384-329f-4aa2-a044-b78a04d6c29a . These are supporting finite numerical data for that contribution, not a theorem or table attributed to Masullo. The theorem proves all real exponential inequalities by rational Taylor estimates, scaling and inversion; the table alone makes no accuracy assertion.

